('en','wichtig_note_ph','What is it about? e.g. gig moved'),
('en','wichtig_hint','Goes out as mail at once — whatever anyone has set for their daily mail.'),
('en','wichtig_confirm','This sends a mail at once to everyone allowed to see the entry. Continue?'),
('en','fl_wichtig_set','Reported as important, the mail is on its way.'),
('en','fl_wichtig_unset','Mark withdrawn.'),
('en','fl_wichtig_already','Was already marked important — no second mail goes out.'),
('en','set_wichtig','Important notices'),
('en','set_wichtig_hint','An entry can be marked as important. That sends a mail at once to everyone allowed to see it — for what cannot wait until the daily mail.'),
('en','set_wichtig_mail','Send an immediate mail when something is marked important'),
('en','set_wichtig_who','Who may mark?'),
('en','set_wichtig_who_write','Whoever could change the entry'),
('en','set_wichtig_who_admin','Band leadership only'),
('en','set_wichtig_who_alle','Anyone who can see it'),
('en','set_wichtig_nooptout','An individual member cannot switch this mail off — otherwise it fails to reach exactly the people who rarely look in. Whoever does not want it at all switches it off here for the whole band.'),
('en','set_wichtig_saved','Important notices saved.'),
('en','help_tagesmail','The daily mail collects what is waiting for you in the band area and sends it to you — meant for everyone who does not look in every day. It holds what you have not looked at yet (the same marks as on the page), unread posts in the chat, your open tasks and dates you have not replied to. Your own changes never appear, and what you are not allowed to see is not in it either.'),
('en','help_tagesmail_2','You set it in your profile under "Daily mail": how often (off, daily, every two days, weekly), from what time of day, and whether it reminds you even when nothing new has come in since the last one. "Off" is a real choice — then nothing comes. If nothing is open, no mail comes anyway. After an update it is off for everyone at first; whoever wants it switches it on.'),
('en','help_tagesmail_3','Every line in the mail leads to the place it is about. If your session has expired, the login comes first and then exactly that entry — you do not have to look for it. The mail is plain text without images so it arrives readable in any program, and the time of day is an earliest: it goes out at the first occasion from your time onwards, not on the minute.'),
('en','help_wichtig','Some things cannot wait for the daily mail: the gig has moved, the rehearsal is off. Marking an entry as important sends a mail at once to everyone allowed to see it — with a line about what it is, and a link straight there. A note like "gig moved" is the reason the mail gets read; without it, it only says something has changed.'),
('en','help_wichtig_2','The band decides in the settings whether these mails exist at all and who may mark, because otherwise the exclamation mark becomes everyday furniture. An individual member cannot switch them off: they would then fail to reach exactly the people who rarely look in. Marking twice sends no second mail, and whoever marks gets none themselves. Withdrawing is possible at any time and sends nothing — taking something back is not news. The button is on the dates and on the tasks; further places can be added with a few lines.'),

